00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.367
the more you save
the whole picnic.

00:08:43.234 --> 00:08:45.334
You save the whole picnic.
You know what I'm saying, Dude?

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:46.734
You can help --
Quest can help with that.

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:48.067
We're gonna make that?
-It just illuminates.

00:08:48.067 --> 00:08:49.200
-Talk to the OFF! people.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.834
-There's, like,
a Thermacell Croc.

00:08:50.834 --> 00:08:53.968
You just -- Yeah, I don't want
to have to spray stuff. Yeah.

00:08:53.968 --> 00:08:55.434
-We just need to combo
two companies together.

00:08:55.434 --> 00:08:57.400
-Out of any of these ideas,
are we doing any of these?

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.934
[ Laughs ] Nothing.
Okay, good.

00:08:58.934 --> 00:09:00.767
-The seven-layer-dip idea,
I think, is good.

00:09:00.767 --> 00:09:02.367
-Alright, good.
-I'm gonna be honest with you.

00:09:02.367 --> 00:09:04.567
-Let's talk about
"Your Place or Mine."

00:09:04.567 --> 00:09:07.434
You, Reese Witherspoon --
that's a home run to me.

00:09:07.434 --> 00:09:09.467
I thought, "Oh --" Right?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:09.467 --> 00:09:11.901
I would watch you guys --
I would watch you guys

00:09:11.901 --> 00:09:13.968
just do nothing and eat lunch,

00:09:13.968 --> 00:09:16.167
but you guys are together
in a romantic comedy.

00:09:16.167 --> 00:09:17.501
-Yeah.
-I love this.

00:09:17.501 --> 00:09:20.567
-Jimmy, I --
So, for however long --

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:22.868
I've done 10 romantic comedies.

00:09:22.868 --> 00:09:25.467
I want to say like
5 out of the ten, I was like --

00:09:25.467 --> 00:09:27.133
I would call my agent
and be like, "Can Reese do it?

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:28.400
Is Reese available?
Should we get Reese?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.667
Can we get Reese?
Can we call Reese?

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:30.901
Can someone -- Does somebody
have Reese's number?

00:09:30.901 --> 00:09:32.934
We should call Reese."
-Yeah.

00:09:32.934 --> 00:09:34.534
-And she was always
working on something else.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:37.434
And, at a point, I was like, "I
just think she doesn't like me."

00:09:37.434 --> 00:09:41.901
And then, actually, in fact,
she recently told me

00:09:41.901 --> 00:09:43.267
a story about how
she thought I was weird

00:09:43.267 --> 00:09:44.734
because I was at
a party one time

00:09:44.734 --> 00:09:47.234
and I was carrying a cooler
around at the party.

00:09:47.234 --> 00:09:49.267
And they're like -- And she was
like, "No, there's a bar there.

00:09:49.267 --> 00:09:50.434
You don't need your own drinks."

00:09:50.434 --> 00:09:52.033
-No, that's cool.
I like that guy.

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:54.534
-Anyway...
-He's fun.

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:55.834
-So -- Yeah.

00:09:55.834 --> 00:09:57.167
-Yeah, this guy's got
his own cooler.

00:09:57.167 --> 00:09:58.300
I would go up to you.
-Just in case. You don't know.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.601
-Ashton, give me a beer, man.

00:09:59.601 --> 00:10:01.868
-Who wants to pay 20 bucks
for a cocktail? Not me.

00:10:01.868 --> 00:10:02.901
-I'm not gonna go to
the bartender.

00:10:02.901 --> 00:10:04.067
I don't even know that guy.

00:10:04.067 --> 00:10:07.334
-Anyway, so, for the
longest time, I was like,

00:10:07.334 --> 00:10:08.634
"Okay, well,
this is not going to happen."

00:10:08.634 --> 00:10:09.968
And then I was like --
I was not sure

00:10:09.968 --> 00:10:11.234
if I wanted to do another movie.

00:10:11.234 --> 00:10:12.701
I didn't know if
I wanted to do anything.

00:10:12.701 --> 00:10:15.133
My agent sent me this thing,
and they're like, "Hey, listen,

00:10:15.133 --> 00:10:18.300
it's Aline Brosh McKenna,
who did 'Devil Wears Prada.'"

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.901
She did "27 Dresses"
and is a good friend of mine.

00:10:20.901 --> 00:10:22.868
And I reached out to her
on every romantic comedy I did

00:10:22.868 --> 00:10:23.868
and I was like, "Hey,
what's wrong with this scene?

00:10:23.868 --> 00:10:25.200
Can you help me out?"

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.234
She was directing it,
and Reese was starring in it.

00:10:27.234 --> 00:10:29.400
And I was like, "Well,
let me stop what I'm doing today

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.467
and read the screenplay."

00:10:30.467 --> 00:10:31.667
-No-brainer.

00:10:31.667 --> 00:10:33.434
-And I read it,
and it was phenomenal.

00:10:33.434 --> 00:10:38.667
And it's about a couple that
are friends for like 20 years

00:10:38.667 --> 00:10:40.100
and then decide that, yeah,

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.501
maybe there's something
romantic here.

00:10:41.501 --> 00:10:43.400
And I was like, "I don't know
anything about that.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:45.200
I've never been in that kind of
relationship in my life."

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.934
-Sound familiar?

00:10:46.934 --> 00:10:48.868
-And so I was like,
"I have to do this movie."

00:10:48.868 --> 00:10:50.868
And then we figured it out
and made it happen.

00:10:50.868 --> 00:10:52.734
It was amazing.
-It's great. It's really fun.

00:10:52.734 --> 00:10:54.133
It's exactly what
you want it to be.

00:10:54.133 --> 00:10:55.601
It's out this Friday.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:10:55.601 --> 00:10:57.267
Here's Ashton Kutcher
and Reese Witherspoon in

00:10:57.267 --> 00:10:58.467
"Your Place or Mine."

00:10:58.467 --> 00:10:59.467
Take a look.

00:10:59.467 --> 00:11:01.367
-Open the freezer.

00:11:02.601 --> 00:11:04.167
-This also says "urgent."

00:11:04.167 --> 00:11:06.367
-Jack loves those casseroles.

00:11:06.367 --> 00:11:07.868
-You know, I could --
I could buy dinner.

00:11:07.868 --> 00:11:10.267
-Peter, I know that you have
a lot of money,

00:11:10.267 --> 00:11:12.267
but I really don't want you
getting him takeout

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:14.300
and things that are fancy.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:18.033
-Yeah, okay, homework and then
frozen [mumbles] for dinner.

00:11:18.033 --> 00:11:20.100
-I know there's something else
I forgot to tell you.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.734
Shoot! I forgot what
I forgot to tell you.

00:11:21.734 --> 00:11:24.434
-Debbie, stop.

00:11:24.434 --> 00:11:26.601
Take a breath.
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:11:26.601 --> 00:11:29.601
♪♪
-Look around.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.200
Yeah.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.467
Enjoy it.

00:11:36.467 --> 00:11:38.667
Call us later.
-Okay.

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:41.000
-Come on. That's -- Come on!

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.033
I want to hug that movie.
I love it.

00:11:43.033 --> 00:11:44.667
Ashton Kutcher, everybody.

00:11:44.667 --> 00:11:46.267
"Your Place or Mine"

00:11:46.267 --> 00:11:48.767
begins streaming this Friday
